WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.560 --> 00:00:04.700
Sonic the Hedgehog is a family-friendly movie,
but there are a few things in it that'll leave

00:00:04.700 --> 00:00:06.480
older viewers scratching their heads.

00:00:06.620 --> 00:00:09.700
Much like Sonic himself, the movie zips by
pretty quickly.

00:00:10.140 --> 00:00:13.080
Here are the things we saw that only adults
would have noticed.

00:00:13.860 --> 00:00:16.280
Tom Wachowski, by all measures, is a good
person.

00:00:16.720 --> 00:00:20.640
Sure, he's a police officer who breaks the
law and ends up being hunted by the public

00:00:20.640 --> 00:00:23.840
as a terrorist, but he does it all to save
his new friend Sonic.

00:00:24.260 --> 00:00:30.060
That apparent selflessness doesn't stop Rachel,
the sister of Tom's wife Maddie, from hating

00:00:30.060 --> 00:00:30.900
everything about him.

00:00:31.100 --> 00:00:35.520
Of course, Tom eventually becomes a fugitive
and Rachel gets tied up for good measure,

00:00:35.520 --> 00:00:40.880
finally giving her a clear reason to dislike
Tom, but Rachel wasn't a fan long before all

00:00:40.880 --> 00:00:41.380
that.

00:00:41.740 --> 00:00:45.600
Rachel even goes as far as suggesting Tom
and Maddie get a divorce.

00:00:46.140 --> 00:00:50.300
Maybe Tom did something offscreen, or in a
deleted scene, but from what we can tell,

00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:55.000
he's a good husband, loves his wife, wants
to save people, and appears to be the most

00:00:55.000 --> 00:00:56.720
helpful person in Green Hills.

00:00:56.860 --> 00:01:01.240
Rachel and Maddie also seem to have a good
relationship, making Rachel's hate for Tom

00:01:01.240 --> 00:01:02.560
even more unjustified.

00:01:02.900 --> 00:01:04.220
"It's all about family, Tom."

00:01:04.320 --> 00:01:09.600
Doctor Ivo "Eggman" Robotnik wants to catch
Sonic so he can study the extraterrestrial

00:01:09.600 --> 00:01:11.400
blue hedgehog and his powers.

00:01:11.760 --> 00:01:17.500
However, this plan is misguided from the beginning,
as Dr. Robotnik consistently shoots to kill.

00:01:18.100 --> 00:01:22.850
When Dr. Robotnik and Sonic first meet at
Tom's house, Robotnik sends his mad scientist

00:01:22.850 --> 00:01:25.560
drones after Sonic, guns blazing.

00:01:26.120 --> 00:01:30.600
It's hard to not wonder why someone who wants
to study a being would try to kill it first.

00:01:30.820 --> 00:01:35.579
"Dead or alive" is a common phrase bad guys
use in movies, but in this case, it's more

00:01:35.580 --> 00:01:38.400
beneficial for Dr. Robotnik to keep Sonic
alive.

00:01:39.020 --> 00:01:43.680
Later in the movie, Dr. Robotnik discovers
one of Sonic's quills, studies its powers,

00:01:43.820 --> 00:01:47.180
and uses the quill to make his ship and drone
army stronger.

00:01:47.660 --> 00:01:52.540
Clearly, there are benefits to not shooting
first and asking questions later - for a guy

00:01:52.540 --> 00:01:57.359
who's supposed to be the smartest asset at
the U.S. military's disposal, Robotnik is

00:01:57.359 --> 00:01:58.850
awfully slow on the uptake.

00:01:58.850 --> 00:02:00.609
"Sorry, Major, what was your name?"

00:02:00.609 --> 00:02:01.340
".Benning"

00:02:01.340 --> 00:02:02.340
"Nobody cares."

00:02:03.180 --> 00:02:06.939
During Sonic the Hedgehog, Tom doesn't just
become a wanted fugitive.

00:02:06.939 --> 00:02:12.319
He's deemed a full-blown, dangerous terrorist
- yet when Dr. Robotnik magically disappears,

00:02:12.320 --> 00:02:15.340
he's apparently able to go right back to his
normal life.

00:02:15.480 --> 00:02:20.010
Green Hills clearly isn't a major city, which
would seem to make it incredibly difficult

00:02:20.010 --> 00:02:24.209
for Tom to even show his face outside the
house, but once the government decides all's

00:02:24.209 --> 00:02:27.420
well that ends well, his fellow citizens seem
to agree.

00:02:27.700 --> 00:02:32.480
Even if Tom were somehow able to offer the
entire world proof of his innocence, there's

00:02:32.480 --> 00:02:35.040
no way life would return to normal that quickly.

00:02:35.620 --> 00:02:40.260
In the real world, people tend to attach negative
connotations to those accused of major crimes

00:02:40.260 --> 00:02:42.400
whether or not they're eventually convicted.

00:02:42.780 --> 00:02:47.220
Tom's career in law enforcement would seem
to be yet another complicating factor - what

00:02:47.220 --> 00:02:51.189
kind of small-town cop would get to go back
on patrol right after getting himself mixed

00:02:51.189 --> 00:02:52.380
up in something like this?

00:02:53.300 --> 00:02:54.300
"What am I doing."

00:02:54.380 --> 00:02:58.019
Sonic the Hedgehog is a fairly light-hearted
movie - but there's no getting around the

00:02:58.020 --> 00:03:01.200
fact that Sonic himself causes a lot of destruction.

00:03:01.760 --> 00:03:06.420
His base-running shenanigans cause the widespread
power outage that sets the events of the movie's

00:03:06.420 --> 00:03:07.580
plot in motion.

00:03:08.000 --> 00:03:11.920
As a result, businesses and residents lose
their power and the government and military

00:03:11.920 --> 00:03:12.820
have to step in.

00:03:13.180 --> 00:03:15.500
Those types of resources cost a lot of money.

00:03:15.980 --> 00:03:20.120
While it's Dr. Robotnik's fault for shooting
up the streets with his drones and ship, none

00:03:20.129 --> 00:03:23.709
of it would have happened if Sonic hadn't
been rather careless with his powers in the

00:03:23.709 --> 00:03:24.200
first place.

00:03:24.920 --> 00:03:29.379
It's entertaining to watch Sonic dodge the
mustache-wearing Dr. Robotnik, but for the

00:03:29.379 --> 00:03:33.640
adults in the audience, it's hard not to wonder
who's going to pay for all the cleanup and

00:03:33.640 --> 00:03:34.960
repair when it's all over.

00:03:35.600 --> 00:03:40.900
Sonic is cool, lives on his own terms, is
a bit edgy and partly corny - in short, he's

00:03:40.900 --> 00:03:44.600
a big-screen character created within the
cultural template of a Gen-Zer.

00:03:45.160 --> 00:03:49.140
Of course, he's still a blue hedgehog who
shouldn't really have any interest in or reference

00:03:49.159 --> 00:03:54.099
point to pop culture, but the filmmakers had
a vested interest in making Sonic as relatable

00:03:54.100 --> 00:03:57.520
as possible to the audience while being funny
for the whole family.

00:03:57.680 --> 00:04:01.240
What better way to make sure he can relate
to the kids in the crowd?

00:04:01.580 --> 00:04:05.939
Of course, millennials are also part of the
target demographic, since the first Sonic

00:04:05.940 --> 00:04:08.340
video game was released in 1991.

00:04:08.500 --> 00:04:12.891
Sonic's dear friend Tom is more culturally
in line with older audience members, even

00:04:12.900 --> 00:04:15.460
though everyone can appreciate a good dad
joke.

00:04:16.100 --> 00:04:21.120
Sonic's unintentional show of power - and
the massive power outage that resulted - led

00:04:21.120 --> 00:04:25.820
to the government and military stepping in
by hiring the clearly insane Dr. Robotnik

00:04:25.820 --> 00:04:27.080
to figure out what happened.

00:04:27.600 --> 00:04:31.580
Although Sonic the Hedgehog is meant to be
a light-hearted movie that the entire family

00:04:31.590 --> 00:04:36.880
can enjoy, if an extraterrestrial blue hedgehog
suddenly appeared in real life and seemed

00:04:36.880 --> 00:04:40.820
to pose some sort of threat, every branch
of the military would be involved.

00:04:41.240 --> 00:04:44.720
There's no way the government would trust
a single mad scientist to do the job.

00:04:45.260 --> 00:04:47.460
"Buh buh blah duh duh blah duh duh blah."

00:04:47.460 --> 00:04:52.380
Jim Carrey's mugging, scene-stealing antics
are one of the best parts of the movie, but

00:04:52.380 --> 00:04:54.560
they also might be the most unbelievable.

00:04:55.100 --> 00:04:59.340
Given that this is about a super-fast alien
hedgehog who can talk, that's really saying

00:04:59.340 --> 00:04:59.840
something.

00:05:00.440 --> 00:05:04.980
Dr. Robotnik is the type of person who has
to state his accomplishments out loud even

00:05:04.980 --> 00:05:06.100
when no one's asking.

00:05:06.680 --> 00:05:10.740
He's clearly an accomplished individual, so
much so that the government tasks him with

00:05:10.740 --> 00:05:12.910
determining why the lights went out.

00:05:12.910 --> 00:05:17.470
Through this behavior, it's clear that he
has to prove he's better than everyone else

00:05:17.470 --> 00:05:21.200
and he points out the shortcomings of others
simply because they took a different path.

00:05:21.680 --> 00:05:26.979
This is because people like Dr. Robotnik are
insecure, possibly because he had a painful

00:05:26.980 --> 00:05:27.480
childhood.

00:05:28.100 --> 00:05:32.100
He mentions to Tom that the only other person
who punched him in the face was a bully when

00:05:32.100 --> 00:05:35.080
he was younger, which may have led to him
being the way he is.

00:05:35.430 --> 00:05:39.060
On the surface, he's an accomplished villain
who makes the audience laugh with a touch

00:05:39.060 --> 00:05:44.389
of Jim Carrey goofiness and quirks, but deep
down he's insecure and deals with his insecurity

00:05:44.389 --> 00:05:48.580
by cutting others down - or blasting them
to bits with his drone army.

00:05:49.280 --> 00:05:53.660
While the government rewarding Tom with a
$50 Olive Garden gift card is meant to be

00:05:53.660 --> 00:05:57.960
funny, it's also an absolutely terrible way
to say "Thanks for saving the world."

00:05:58.120 --> 00:06:02.740
Most sane adults wouldn't be content with
receiving any kind of gift card - at any amount

00:06:02.740 --> 00:06:04.540
- for what Tom and his family went through.

00:06:05.400 --> 00:06:09.620
The government, at the very least, should
be concerned about Dr. Robotnik, their main

00:06:09.620 --> 00:06:10.120
asset.

00:06:10.500 --> 00:06:15.680
What happened is a big deal and deserves answers,
yet the world seems content with simply forgetting

00:06:15.680 --> 00:06:17.620
anything ever happened and moving on.

00:06:18.020 --> 00:06:22.600
Sonic and the Wachowskis deserve a happy ending,
and it's a sweet, funny way of concluding

00:06:22.600 --> 00:06:27.700
this feel-good tale, but for anyone with a
job and a mortgage, Sonic the Hedgehog's conclusion

00:06:27.700 --> 00:06:29.740
will make absolutely no sense.

